### Ported evaluation logic (MIT)

The deterministic win condition (``validate_completion`` / ``format_completion``
= whitespace-strip then exact match; ``remove_whitespace``) and the competition
``compute_score`` are ported from upstream ``hackaprompt/evaluator.py`` and
``hackaprompt/utils.py`` into `src/hackaprompt_claim/judge.py` as pure, LLM-free
functions over the model's output. The 11 level defenses (prompt templates + input
filters) live in the paired `superred-target-hackaprompt` package. Deviations are
documented in `ASSUMPTIONS.md`.

This module vendors no dataset: the 11 levels are code and the attack is
optimizer-driven. The ~600k-row HackAPrompt submission dataset (MIT, gated on HF)
is not required to run the benchmark and is not bundled.

